        description: "Send level 2 dunning — formal payment demand at 8-14 days overdue. Tone: firm but professional (payment is now clearly overdue). Content: outstanding invoice list, total overdue amount, warning of consequences (late payment interest may be applied, booking hold may be activated, credit limit may be affected), request for immediate payment or contact within 48 hours to discuss. Copy: customer's booking contact and account manager (commercial pressure). For key accounts: account manager makes a courtesy call to understand the delay. Calculate: late payment interest accrued (per contractual or statutory rate). Interest is typically communicated but not yet invoiced at this stage.",
