        description: "Authorize commencement of legal proceedings if payment not received after legal notice period. Decision factors: debt amount vs expected legal costs (litigation is expensive — typically only justified for debts >$25,000), customer's financial status (is the customer solvent? No point suing an insolvent company), jurisdiction (enforcing judgments across borders is complex and costly), evidence strength (is our claim well-documented?), and commercial relationship (are we prepared to end this relationship?). Alternatives to litigation: mediation, arbitration (if contract specifies), or debt collection agency. Authority: CFO approval for legal action. Engage external legal counsel for proceedings.",
