        description: "Post journal entries for approved bad debt write-off. Accounting treatment: debit bad debt expense account (or debit allowance for doubtful debts if provision already existed), credit accounts receivable (remove the debt from AR). If provision was previously booked: reverse provision (debit allowance, credit provision expense) and book write-off separately for clarity. For insurance recovery received: debit cash, credit bad debt recovery income. Ensure: write-off reduces AR aging (no longer shows as overdue), customer credit limit adjustment (may reduce permanently), and management reporting reflects the write-off. Archive all write-off documentation for minimum 7 years (audit retention requirement).",
