        description: "Continuous monitoring of all critical L/C dates to prevent expiry or missed deadlines. Track: (1) Latest shipment date — the BL on-board date must be on or before this date, alert operations 14/7/3 days before; (2) L/C expiry date — all documents must be presented to the bank before this date, alert 21/14/7 days before; (3) Document presentation period — UCP 600 allows 21 days from BL date to present documents (but L/C may specify shorter, e.g., 14 days); (4) Payment due date — for deferred payment L/Cs, track maturity date for cash flow forecasting; (5) Amendment deadlines — if amendments are pending, track response timelines. Generate daily dashboard showing all active L/Cs with RAG status: GREEN (>14 days to nearest deadline), AMBER (7-14 days), RED (<7 days). Auto-escalate RED items to trade finance manager. Cross-reference against vessel schedule changes — if a vessel is delayed, immediately flag impact on L/C shipment date.",
