        description: "Discharge OOG/break-bulk cargo at destination port using specialized equipment. Reverse of loading process: remove lashings and securing, rig for lift, discharge to quay or directly to transport. Special considerations at discharge: cargo condition survey before de-lashing (document any transit damage for claims), crane availability (must be pre-arranged if shore crane needed), laydown area on quay (for break-bulk staging), and immediate transport availability (to minimize port dwell and risk). For heavy lifts: same weather and safety protocols as loading. Chief officer releases cargo only when surveyor confirms condition.",
