        description: "Allocate repositioning costs to the trade lanes that caused the imbalance. Principle: the trade lane that generates empty surplus (typically the import-heavy direction) bears the repo cost of moving empties to where they are needed. Allocation methods: per-TEU allocation based on imbalance ratio, or direct attribution to specific trade lanes. This ensures trade lane P&L reflects true cost including equipment repositioning.",
