        description: "Build a detailed Profit & Loss projection for the proposed service on the target trade lane. Revenue model: forecast freight revenue per TEU by container type (dry 20/40, reefer 20/40, special) using market rate intelligence (Freightos Baltic Index, Xeneta, Drewry WCI for benchmarks), multiplied by projected volume from step 1. Add ancillary revenue: THC (Terminal Handling Charges), documentation fees, B/L fees, seal charges, demurrage/detention income, VGM weighing fees, container cleaning charges — typically 15-25% of freight revenue. Cost model: vessel operating costs (crew, insurance, maintenance, management fee — typically $6,000-$12,000/day depending on vessel size), fuel costs (bunker consumption at eco-speed × IFO380/VLSFO/LSMGO prices from Ship & Bunker), port costs (pilotage, towage, berth hire, canal dues per port call — use standard port tariffs), terminal handling costs (loading/discharge per TEU move), container costs (lease rate per CEU/day for owned vs leased fleet, repositioning costs for empty containers — a major cost driver, typically 30-40% of container fleet repositioning), agency fees, and overhead allocation. Calculate contribution margin per TEU, break-even load factor (typically 50-65% for liner services), NPV over 3-5 year horizon at company WACC, and IRR. Sensitivity analysis on: bunker price ±20%, freight rate ±15%, volume ±10%.",
