        description: "Calculate the precise vessel requirement for the approved service. The fundamental formula: vessels_required = ceil(round_voyage_days / frequency_days) + spare_factor. For a 42-day round voyage with weekly (7-day) frequency: 42/7 = 6 vessels minimum. Add spare factor for: dry dock windows (each vessel needs ~15 days every 2.5 years for intermediate survey, ~30 days every 5 years for special survey), schedule buffer (2-3 days per rotation to absorb weather delays, port congestion, and canal waiting), and peak season extra loaders. Calculate vessel specification requirements: minimum TEU capacity (based on demand × target utilization of 75-85%), maximum draft restriction (constrained by shallowest port on rotation — e.g., if Nhava Sheva at 14m, vessel must be <14m loaded draft), LOA restriction (constrained by smallest berth/lock on route), reefer plug count (based on reefer demand %), gear requirement (geared vessels needed if any port lacks shore cranes), and speed requirement (minimum speed to maintain schedule at eco-steaming — typically 14-18 knots for container vessels). Factor in CII (Carbon Intensity Indicator) compliance — vessels must achieve at least C rating; older vessels at D/E rating need speed reduction or technical modifications. Output: vessel technical specification matrix and number of vessels required with spare vessel strategy.",
