        description: "Select and assign specific vessels from the company's own fleet to the new service. The AI agent matches available vessels against the technical specification from step 10, considering: current deployment status (vessel must be available — not committed to another service without replacement), vessel condition and age (prefer vessels with recent dry dock, good CII rating), fuel efficiency (lower SFOC = lower bunker cost per voyage), crew readiness (manning level, certification currency), and commercial suitability (customer preferences — some major BCOs specify vessel age/flag requirements in contracts). Optimization algorithm considers fleet-wide redeployment: reassigning a vessel from service A to the new service B may create a gap on A that can be filled by a smaller/different vessel from service C, creating a cascade of moves. The agent models these cascading moves and finds the optimal fleet-wide deployment that minimizes total repositioning cost and maximizes overall fleet utilization. If fewer own vessels are available than required, the gap is flagged for charter-in (step 12). Output: vessel assignment plan with named vessels, repositioning voyage plan from current location to first loading port, and fleet gap count (if any).",
