        description: "Perform comprehensive fleet financial assessment for the confirmed vessel deployment. Calculate Time Charter Equivalent (TCE) — the industry-standard metric for comparing vessel earnings: TCE = (Gross Revenue − Voyage Costs) / Operating Days. Voyage costs include: bunker (largest variable cost — calculate consumption at eco-speed per leg × bunker price), port charges (pilotage, towage, berth hire per port call), canal dues (Suez Canal tolls based on SCNT measurement, typically $200,000-$700,000 per transit for container vessels), terminal handling costs, and agency fees. For each vessel (owned and chartered): calculate daily operating cost (owned: depreciation + OPEX + finance cost; chartered: hire rate), daily break-even revenue requirement, and break-even load factor. Model fleet-level economics: total deployment cost per round voyage, revenue per round voyage at target utilization, contribution to company overhead, and payback period for repositioning investment. Compare TCE against market TC rates — if TCE < market TC rate, the vessel earns less than if it were chartered out, flagging potential misallocation. Produce fleet deployment financial summary for the approval gate.",
