        module: "Canal", step: "Canal transit planning — Suez/Panama (if applicable)", type: "ai", executorType: "ai_agent", phase: "Schedule Creation", condition: "route_includes_canal === true", moduleUrl: "/schedule-voyage-planning/canal-transits/new",
        description: "Plan canal transit logistics for services that route through the Suez Canal or Panama Canal. Suez Canal (most common for Middle East services): calculate transit fees based on Suez Canal Net Tonnage (SCNT) — Suez Canal Authority (SCA) publishes annual tariff tables, container vessels pay based on laden TEU count + SCNT; typical cost: $200,000-$700,000 per transit depending on vessel size. Plan convoy joining times — northbound convoy departs from Suez at 03:00-04:00, southbound from Port Said at 06:00-07:00; vessels must arrive at convoy anchorage 4-6 hours before departure. Transit takes 12-16 hours through the 193km canal. Since 2015 expansion, the New Suez Canal allows two-way traffic in the central section, reducing waiting time. Plan for pilot boarding, tugboat assistance (mandatory for large container vessels), and canal documentation (transit papers, crew list, cargo declaration). Panama Canal (for services connecting Pacific/Atlantic): two options — Panamax locks (max 5,000 TEU, beam ≤32.3m) or Neopanamax locks (max 14,000 TEU, beam ≤51.25m). Booking system: auction slots (premium for guaranteed transit date) vs regular slots (may wait 1-7 days). Transit fee: $100,000-$800,000 depending on vessel size and lock type. Plan fresh water fee (Gatun Lake draft restrictions during dry season).",
