        module: "Speed/Fuel", step: "Speed & fuel analysis per leg", type: "ai", executorType: "ai_agent", phase: "Schedule Creation", moduleUrl: "/schedule-voyage-planning/speed-fuel-analyses",
        description: "Perform detailed speed and fuel analysis for every leg on the rotation. For each leg (port A → port B): calculate optimal speed considering the schedule window (time available = ETD port A to ETA port B minus pilot boarding time), distance, weather conditions (seasonal: SW monsoon Jun-Sep in Indian Ocean adds 5-10% to consumption, NE monsoon Nov-Feb adds 3-5%), and current (favorable or adverse — Red Sea/Suez approach has strong northerly currents). Determine fuel type per leg: within ECA (Emission Control Areas) — if any ports are in ECA zones (currently North Sea, Baltic, North America, US Caribbean), vessel must burn LSMGO (0.10% sulfur) or have scrubber; outside ECA: VLSFO (0.50% sulfur) or HFO (3.50% sulfur with scrubber). Calculate bunker consumption per leg using vessel-specific SFOC (Specific Fuel Oil Consumption) curves — consumption increases exponentially with speed (roughly: doubling speed = 8× fuel consumption). At eco-speed (14-16 knots for typical container vessel), consumption is typically 80-120 MT/day for 4,000-8,000 TEU vessels. Calculate total bunker cost per round voyage using bunker prices at planned bunkering ports (prices vary significantly — Singapore typically cheapest, Middle East competitive, Mediterranean premium). Optimize speed per leg to minimize fuel cost while maintaining schedule — if a leg has slack time, slow down to save bunker (slow steaming).",
