        module: "Validation", step: "Schedule quality validation (transit time, competitiveness, feasibility)", type: "ai", processRef: "PRC-042", executorType: "ai_agent", phase: "Schedule Creation",
        description: "Comprehensive quality validation of the complete schedule before publication. Three validation dimensions: (1) Transit Time Competitiveness — compare port-to-port and door-to-door transit times against competitor services on the same trade lane (from step 2 competitive assessment). For key port pairs, transit time must be within 10% of best competitor or offer compensating advantage (price, reliability, direct vs transshipment). Flag any port pair where transit time is >20% worse than best alternative. (2) Schedule Feasibility — verify the entire 52-week schedule is physically executable: no speed violations (already checked in step 18), adequate port time for expected moves (crane productivity × moves ÷ cranes ≥ port stay duration), canal convoy alignment, tidal window compliance at draft-restricted ports, and berth window adherence. Simulate schedule disruption scenarios: what happens if a vessel is 24/48 hours late at one port? Model the cascade effect and recovery plan (speed up on next leg, reduce port time, skip port if severe). (3) Operational Consistency — validate that the schedule pattern is consistent week-to-week (customers expect same day/time arrivals), that seasonal adjustments (monsoon speed reduction) are built in, and that dry dock windows are covered (replacement vessel schedules). Generate a Schedule Quality Score (0-100) based on weighted criteria.",
