        description: "Allocate vessel capacity across commercial channels for each sailing. Total vessel capacity (e.g., 4,500 TEU nominal, ~4,000 TEU effective after weight/stability constraints) must be allocated across: (1) Contract/NAC (Named Account Contract) — capacity reserved for major BCO (Beneficial Cargo Owner) customers under annual contracts with committed volumes and agreed rates. Typically 40-60% of capacity. Allocate based on customer contract MQC (Minimum Quantity Commitment) prorated per sailing; (2) Spot market — capacity available for ad-hoc bookings at prevailing market rates. Typically 20-35% of capacity. Pricing is dynamic based on utilization (higher rates when vessel is filling up); (3) Alliance/VSA slots — capacity allocated to alliance partners per VSA agreement (from step 8). Typically 10-30% if service is a VSA; (4) Reefer — dedicated reefer plug allocation (reefer plugs are a constrained resource — vessel may have 4,500 TEU but only 500 reefer plugs). Allocate reefer across contract/spot proportionally; (5) Special cargo — reserve slots for OOG (out-of-gauge), hazardous, and heavy-lift cargo requiring specific stowage positions. The AI agent optimizes allocation to maximize revenue: contract cargo provides base load certainty, spot cargo captures upside in strong markets, and alliance slots fulfill partnership obligations. Allocation is per sailing, per direction (outbound/inbound), per port pair segment.",
