        description: "Configure cargo cut-off rules for each port on the rotation. Cut-offs define the deadlines by which cargo, documentation, and VGM (Verified Gross Mass) must be submitted — after cut-off, no further bookings or cargo acceptance for that sailing. Three types of cut-off: (1) Physical/Cargo Cut-Off — deadline for container to arrive at terminal gate. Typically 24-48 hours before ETD. Varies by port: Jebel Ali often 24h, Nhava Sheva 48h, European ports 24h. Terminal-specific — some terminals have different cut-offs for different berths; (2) Documentation Cut-Off — deadline for shipping instructions (SI), customs declarations, and cargo manifest submission. Typically 48-72 hours before ETD. Earlier in ports with strict customs requirements (e.g., US 24-hour advance manifest rule per CBP, EU ICS2 pre-loading advance cargo information); (3) VGM Cut-Off — deadline for Verified Gross Mass submission per SOLAS regulation (mandatory since July 2016). Typically 24 hours before ETD. Two methods: Method 1 (weigh packed container) or Method 2 (calculate from cargo + packaging + container tare weight). Configure cut-off rules per port with: standard offset from ETD (e.g., physical = ETD minus 24h), exceptions for specific cargo types (reefer may have later cut-off due to last-minute loading), holiday adjustments (if cut-off falls on port holiday, move to previous working day), and system enforcement (booking system blocks acceptance after cut-off, EDI rejection for late SI/VGM).",
