        description: "Monthly analysis of route optimization opportunities based on accumulated operational data. After 3-6 months of service operation, sufficient data exists to validate or challenge the original service design assumptions. Analyze: (1) Port call value — for each port on the rotation, calculate the net contribution (revenue generated from cargo loaded/discharged minus port costs, terminal charges, and time cost of the port call). Identify ports where net contribution is negative — candidates for port omission or reduced frequency; (2) Transit time optimization — based on actual speed and weather data, identify legs where schedule can be tightened (faster transit, shorter port stay) or needs relaxation (add buffer where delays are frequent); (3) Port addition opportunities — based on bookings that are being transshipped (indicating demand from non-direct ports), identify ports that could be added to the rotation to capture direct cargo; (4) Seasonal schedule adjustment — analyze seasonal volume patterns and recommend: summer schedule (potentially add port call during peak), winter schedule (potentially omit low-volume port, slow-steam to save bunker); (5) Competition response — if competitor has launched/withdrawn service on overlapping route, recommend adjustments. Output a monthly route optimization report with recommended modifications ranked by financial impact.",
