        description: "Periodic service review gate (quarterly or triggered by performance alerts) where senior management decides the service's future. Review the complete performance package: schedule reliability trend, load factor trend, revenue per TEU trend, actual vs budget P&L, route optimization recommendations, demand forecast outlook, and competitive landscape changes. Decision options: (1) Continue unchanged — service is performing at or above expectations, no modifications needed; (2) Modify — implement specific changes such as port addition/omission, frequency change (weekly to fortnightly or vice versa), vessel swap (larger/smaller based on demand), rate adjustment, or rotation resequencing. Modification requires formal change request flowing back through relevant steps (network design, terminal negotiation, schedule revision); (3) Suspend — temporarily halt the service due to seasonal low demand, geopolitical disruption (e.g., Red Sea/Houthi crisis forcing Suez Canal avoidance in 2024-2025), or vessel reallocation to higher-priority service. Suspension maintains service identity for restart; (4) Retire — permanently discontinue the service. Triggers: customer notification (minimum 30-60 days advance), booking rundown (stop accepting new bookings, honor existing), final voyage execution, terminal agreement termination, rate withdrawal, and capacity reallocation. This gate may also make ad-hoc decisions: blank sailing (cancel a specific sailing due to low demand — save bunker/port costs), extra loader (add a sailing due to overflow demand), or port omission (skip a port on specific voyage due to congestion/weather).",
