        description: "Generate statement of cash flows per IAS 7. Three sections: operating activities (indirect method — net profit adjusted for non-cash items and working capital changes), investing activities (vessel acquisitions/disposals, container purchases, capex), and financing activities (borrowings drawn/repaid, lease payments, dividends paid). For shipping: operating cash flow is critical metric — investors focus on cash generation from operations before fleet investment. Handle: FX impact on cash and cash equivalents, restricted cash (deposits, escrow), and non-cash investing/financing activities (disclosed in notes). Reconcile opening to closing cash balance.",
