        description: "Physical receipt and inspection of goods at delivery point (warehouse, office, or vessel). Receiver verifies: items match PO description, quantity matches PO (count or weigh), condition is acceptable (no damage, correct packaging), and quality meets specifications (visual inspection, or lab test for technical items). For vessel stores delivered at port: ship's officer receives, checks against PO and delivery note, and signs goods receipt. For technical items (engine parts, safety equipment): may require technical officer inspection. Document: delivery note number, received quantity, condition, and any discrepancies. Short deliveries or damaged items: note on receipt and notify procurement for vendor follow-up.",
