        description: "Update inventory records based on goods receipt. For warehoused items: add to inventory with location (warehouse, shelf, bin), update stock levels, and check if receipt satisfies pending demand (back-orders or maintenance work orders waiting for parts). For vessel stores: update vessel-specific inventory (each vessel maintains its own stores inventory for spares, consumables, provisions). Trigger: reorder point alerts (if receipt brings stock above reorder point — cancel any pending reorder), and expiry tracking (for items with shelf life — chemicals, provisions, medical supplies). Post accounting entry: debit inventory account, credit goods received not invoiced (GRNI) accrual account.",
