        description: "Review and resolve invoices with three-way match discrepancies or validation flags. Common discrepancies: price variance (vendor charged different from PO — may be legitimate price adjustment or error), quantity variance (received more/less than invoiced), missing GRN (goods received but receipt not yet entered — chase receiver), and tax discrepancy. Resolution options: accept variance (if justified — e.g., price increase notification received), request credit note from vendor, hold payment pending investigation, or reject invoice and return to vendor. For fraud flags: escalate to finance controller/internal audit. Document resolution for audit trail.",
