        description: "Claims manager reviews the incident investigation report and classifies the severity level, which determines the claims handling pathway. Severity levels: (1) MINOR (estimated <USD 10,000) — handle in-house with standard documentation, no survey required unless disputed; (2) MODERATE (USD 10,000-100,000) — appoint independent surveyor, notify P&I Club correspondent, follow standard claims procedure; (3) MAJOR (USD 100,000-1M) — immediate P&I Club notification, appoint specialist surveyor and legal counsel, establish claims reserve, management oversight; (4) CATASTROPHIC (>USD 1M or General Average) — full crisis response team, P&I Club leads, board notification, potential General Average declaration. Decision also covers: whether to appoint surveyor (mandatory for moderate+), which surveyor firm to use (from approved panel), whether legal counsel needed, initial liability position (admit, deny, or investigate further), and whether to invoke any cargo insurance policy the company holds.",
