        description: "Register the formal claim in the claims management system with all required details. Capture: (1) Claim reference number (auto-generated); (2) Claimant details (shipper, consignee, or cargo insurer as subrogated party); (3) Claim type — physical damage, shortage, contamination, delay, misdelivery, temperature deviation; (4) BL number(s) and booking reference(s); (5) Container number(s) and seal condition; (6) Cargo description, declared value, and commercial invoice value; (7) Basis of claim — Hague-Visby Rules (carrier liability limited to 2 SDR per kilo or 666.67 SDR per package, whichever higher), Hamburg Rules, or contractual terms; (8) Time bar status — Hague-Visby requires suit within 1 year of delivery (or when goods should have been delivered), track this critical deadline; (9) Supporting documents received (survey report, commercial invoice, BL, packing list, photos); (10) Link to incident investigation record. Set up the claims docket with milestones and deadlines. Auto-calculate the Hague-Visby limitation amount based on cargo weight and package count.",
