        description: "Appoint an independent cargo surveyor from the approved panel to inspect the damaged cargo and provide an impartial assessment. Selection criteria: (1) Surveyor must be independent (not employed by either party); (2) Qualification — IICL certified for containers, appropriate commodity expertise for cargo; (3) Geographical availability — must be able to reach the cargo location within 48 hours; (4) P&I Club approval — for large claims, the P&I Club may insist on their preferred surveyor; (5) Joint survey preference — invite the claimant's surveyor to participate for transparency. Notify claimant of survey date/time/location. The survey must happen before cargo is disposed of, repaired, or moved (this is critical — if cargo is disposed of without survey, liability becomes harder to contest). For perishable cargo, expedited survey within 24 hours. Issue formal survey appointment letter with scope of inspection.",
