        description: "Compile and validate the complete claims docket documentation. A properly documented claim requires: (1) Original claim letter from claimant; (2) Bill of Lading (original or copy); (3) Commercial invoice showing cargo value; (4) Packing list; (5) Survey report (preliminary and final); (6) Photographs (indexed); (7) Temperature logs (reefer claims); (8) Mate's receipt / tally sheets; (9) Container inspection report (at origin and destination); (10) Weather logs and sea protest (if force majeure defense); (11) Stowage plan and lashing certificates; (12) Carrier's letter of protest to stevedores (if terminal damage); (13) Customs examination report (if shortage claim); (14) Previous cargo certificates (container cleanliness). Track document completeness — flag missing critical documents. For each document, record: date received, source, original/copy status. Documents must support the defense strategy: if contesting liability, ensure all exculpatory evidence is preserved.",
