        module: "ESG", step: "Carbon footprint calculation (fleet-wide)", type: "ai", processRef: "PRC-188", executorType: "ai_agent", phase: "Data Collection", moduleUrl: "/sustainability-esg-reporting/carbon-footprints",
        description: "Calculate the total organizational carbon footprint across all operations (not just vessels). This extends beyond vessel emissions to include: (1) Scope 1 direct — vessel fuel combustion (from step 2), company vehicle fleet, owned buildings heating/cooling; (2) Scope 2 indirect — purchased electricity for offices, ports, terminals, data centers; (3) Scope 3 value chain — upstream fuel production (well-to-tank), business travel (flights, hotels), employee commuting, purchased goods and services, container manufacturing and disposal, port handling (stevedoring energy), inland transport (trucking, rail), waste disposal from vessels and offices. Apply appropriate emission factors from recognized sources: IEA for electricity grids (country-specific), DEFRA for UK operations, EPA for US operations. Calculate total carbon footprint in CO2e (CO2 equivalent, including CH4 and N2O converted using GWP). Present as absolute emissions (tonnes CO2e) and intensity metrics (CO2e per TEU shipped, per revenue USD).",
