        description: "Fleet operations director reviews all D and E rated vessels from the CII calculation and approves corrective action plans. Per IMO regulations, D-rated vessels must develop a corrective action plan within 3 years and E-rated vessels must develop one immediately. The corrective plan must be included in the Ship Energy Efficiency Management Plan (SEEMP Part III). Review includes: (1) Root cause analysis — why is the vessel rated D/E (speed profile, route inefficiency, hull condition, engine performance, age/design); (2) Technical measures — hull cleaning, propeller polishing, energy-saving devices (bulbous bow retrofit, Mewis duct, rotor sails); (3) Operational measures — speed optimization, weather routing, trim optimization, port turnaround reduction; (4) Commercial measures — route redeployment to shorter routes, cargo optimization for better utilization, consider vessel sale/scrap if CII improvement is not economically viable; (5) Financial impact — cost of corrective measures vs penalty of continued D/E rating (future commercial disadvantage as charterers increasingly demand CII A/B vessels).",
