        description: "Notify the flag state administration of the crew change as required by flag state regulations. Different flag states have varying notification requirements: (1) Crew change report — most flag states require notification of crew changes within 48-72 hours, including joining/departing crew details, positions, certificates, and nationalities; (2) Continuous Synopsis Record (CSR) — SOLAS requires the CSR to be updated with crew-related changes if they affect the minimum safe manning; (3) Flag state endorsement verification — some registries require notification when crew with their endorsements join/leave; (4) Manning level reports — flag states may require periodic manning level reports to confirm compliance with safe manning document; (5) Nationality ratio compliance — some flags require minimum percentage of nationals in crew (e.g., some Gulf states require a minimum local crew percentage). Submit notifications via flag state online portal or email as required.",
