        description: "Calculate and process final leave pay entitlement for departing crew. MLC 2006 Regulation 2.4 provides for minimum 2.5 calendar days of annual leave per month of service. Calculate: (1) Leave entitlement — per SEA/CBA terms (typically 8-12 days per month of service depending on rank and CBA); (2) Leave earned during this contract — sign-on to sign-off period; (3) Leave already taken (if any shore leave was granted during contract); (4) Carried forward balance (from previous contracts, if company policy permits); (5) Leave pay rate — basic wage plus fixed allowances per CBA; (6) Payment method — some CBAs require leave pay to be paid in advance, others upon completion of leave; (7) Pro-rata calculation for partial months. Also calculate: end-of-contract bonus (if applicable per CBA), completion bonus, and any loyalty/retention payments. Generate final settlement statement showing: final wages, leave pay, bonuses, less advances and deductions, net amount payable. Process payment to crew member's nominated bank account.",
