        description: "Configure the EDI (Electronic Data Interchange) and API integration layer for the tenant's external connectivity. Container shipping is heavily EDI-dependent — shipping lines exchange standardized EDIFACT messages with terminals, customs authorities, customers, and partners. Key EDI message types to configure: BAPLIE (bayplan/stowage), COPARN (container gate-in/gate-out order), COREOR (container release order), IFTMIN (booking request), IFTSTA (shipment status), INVOIC (commercial invoice), CUSCAR (customs cargo report), CUSRES (customs response), MOVINS (stowage instruction), CODECO (container gate-in/gate-out report), and DESTIM (damage/equipment status). For each trading partner, configure: communication channel (AS2, SFTP, API, email), message format (EDIFACT D95B/D16B, XML, JSON, flat file), partner identification (SCAC code, DUNS number), acknowledgment handling (CONTRL/APERAK), and retry/error handling. Set up customs integration per operating country: Qatar (QNBOD/ASYCUDA), UAE (Mirsal2/Dubai Trade), KSA (FASAH/ZATCA), India (ICEGATE). Configure carrier API integrations for vessel tracking (AIS), container tracking (BIC/DCSA Track & Trace), and financial messaging (SWIFT MT103/MT940 for bank payments). All integrations must support tenant isolation — messages are routed and stored per-tenant, never cross-tenant.",
