        description: "Automated backup management system covering all critical data stores. Database backups: full PostgreSQL backup via pg_dump daily at 02:00 UTC (during lowest traffic window), WAL (Write-Ahead Log) continuous archiving for point-in-time recovery (PITR) with 30-day retention. Each backup is compressed (gzip), encrypted (AES-256), and uploaded to S3 with server-side encryption (SSE-S3). Backup naming convention: {tenant_id}/{date}/{type}_{timestamp}.sql.gz.enc. Redis backups: RDB snapshot every 6 hours + AOF continuous persistence. Document storage: S3 cross-region replication for disaster recovery (primary: me-south-1 Bahrain, secondary: ap-south-1 Mumbai). Backup verification: automated restore test weekly — restore latest backup to test database, run integrity checks (row count comparison, checksum verification on critical tables), and report results. Retention policy: daily backups retained 30 days, weekly backups retained 90 days, monthly backups retained 1 year. Backup size monitoring: alert if backup size grows >20% week-over-week (potential data anomaly). Support manual on-demand backup before major operations (migrations, upgrades). All backup operations logged with start time, duration, size, checksum, and success/failure status.",
